Expected elements: present

The identity bar carries the truncated hash, `block 63675`, both stepping directions, `128 / 345`, the phase rail and an exit that lands on `aztec-testnet`. The provenance marker is the first row of the Transaction pane — `DATA`, a `Real Aztec testnet data` badge, and the capture's own endpoint, moment and replay window. No band above the identity bar. Code, Call Trace and Values each explain the missing symbols in their own words; `Supply sources` is present. No invented source, no fixture content, no engine banner, no unexplained blank pane. The replay telemetry is not visible in the 1080px viewport (finding 1), but the pane is a scroll region populated from real chain facts and its `RAW (CHAIN-NATIVE)` block is visibly mid-object, so I do not score it absent.

On density the page is inverted. 1551px of width — Code, Call Trace, Values — carries six sentences and a button; the 369px Transaction pane carries everything else and runs off the bottom edge. Removing the band gave every pane ~190px, and the pane that needed it spent ~320px of it on a right-aligned sentence block, so the only pane with more content than height came out behind.

Highest-priority fixes: widen the Transaction pane (or move provenance prose to full pane width, left-aligned) so the faithfulness telemetry is on screen; format the fee.

Rating: 6/10

